    20	## Schema compilation and caching
    21	
    22	- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool and retains the compiler error as its cause ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema when registering its tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L11), [validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
    23	- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema`.
